# text = I doubted not -- never doubted -- that if Mr . Reed had been alive he would have treated me kindly ; and now , as I sat looking at the white bed and overshadowed walls -- occasionally also turning a fascinated eye towards the dimly gleaning mirror -- I began to recall what I had heard of dead men , troubled in their graves by the violation of their last wishes , revisiting the earth to punish the perjured and avenge the oppressed ; and I thought Mr . Reed's spirit , harassed by the wrongs of his sister's child , might quit its abode -- whether in the church vault or in the unknown world of the departed -- and rise before me in this chamber .
