# text = Then my sole relief was to walk along the corridor of the third storey , backwards and forwards , safe in the silence and solitude of the spot , and allow my mind's eye to dwell on whatever bright visions rose before it -- and , certainly , they were many and glowing ; to let my heart be heaved by the exultant movement , which , while it swelled it in trouble , expanded it with life ; and , best of all , to open my inward ear to a tale that was never ended -- a tale my imagination created , and narrated continuously ; quickened with all of incident , life , fire , feeling , that I desired and had not in my actual existence .
