# text = I am sure most people would have thought him an ugly man ; yet there was so much unconscious pride in his port ; so much ease in his demeanour ; such a look of complete indifference to his own external appearance ; so haughty a reliance on the power of other qualities , intrinsic or adventitious , to atone for the lack of mere personal attractiveness , that , in looking at him , one inevitably shared the indifference , and , even in a blind , imperfect sense , put faith in the confidence he repeated Instead of speaking , I smiled ; and not a very complacent or submissive smile either he urged Accordingly I sat and said nothing I thought I was dumb still .
