# text = It was his nature to be communicative ; he liked to open to a mind unacquainted with the world glimpses of its scenes and ways ( I do not mean its corrupt scenes and wicked ways , but such as derived their interest from the great scale on which they were acted , the strange novelty by which they were characterised ); and I had a keen delight in receiving the new ideas he offered , in imagining the new pictures he portrayed , and following him in thought through the new regions he disclosed , never startled or troubled by one noxious allusion .
