# text = His eye , as I have often said , was a black eye : it had now a tawny , nay , a bloody light in its gloom ; and his face flushed -- olive cheek and hueless forehead received a glow as from spreading , ascending heart-fire : and he stirred , lifted his strong arm -- he could have struck Mason , dashed him on the church-floor , shocked by ruthless blow the breath from his body -- but Mason shrank away , and cried faintly Contempt fell cool on Mr . Rochester -- his passion died as if a blight had shrivelled it up : he only asked An inaudible reply escaped Mason's white lips interrupted the clergyman Then addressing Mason , he inquired gently urged the lawyer said Mason , in more articulate tones ejaculated the clergyman I saw a grim smile contort Mr . Rochester's lips , and he muttered He mused -- for ten minutes he held counsel with himself : he formed his resolve , and announced it The man obeyed .
