# text = A Christmas frost had come at midsummer ; a white December storm had whirled over June ; ice glazed the ripe apples , drifts crushed the blowing roses ; on hayfield and cornfield lay a frozen shroud : lanes which last night blushed full of flowers , to-day were pathless with untrodden snow ; and the woods , which twelve hours since waved leafy and flagrant as groves between the tropics , now spread , waste , wild , and white as pine-forests in wintry Norway .
