# text = I wrestled with my own resolution : I wanted to be weak that I might avoid the awful passage of further suffering I saw laid out for me ; and Conscience , turned tyrant , held Passion by the throat , told her tauntingly , she had yet but dipped her dainty foot in the slough , and swore that with that arm of iron he would thrust her down to unsounded depths of agony then I cried I rose up suddenly , terror-struck at the solitude which so ruthless a judge haunted , -- at the silence which so awful a voice filled .
