# text = They clung to the purple moors behind and around their dwelling -- to the hollow vale into which the pebbly bridle-path leading from their gate descended , and which wound between fern-banks first , and then amongst a few of the wildest little pasture-fields that ever bordered a wilderness of heath , or gave sustenance to a flock of grey moorland sheep , with their little mossy-faced lambs :- they clung to this scene , I say , with a perfect enthusiasm of attachment .
