# text = I was sure St . John Rivers -- pure-lived , conscientious , zealous as he was -- had not yet found that peace of God which passeth all understanding : he had no more found it , I thought , than had I with my concealed and racking regrets for my broken idol and lost elysium -- regrets to which I have latterly avoided referring , but which possessed me and tyrannised over me ruthlessly .
